/*
Your report should include:

Title Page: Title page should have the following:
Title
Team name
Team member names
Course name: CIS 4914 Senior Project
Name of advisor
Advisor's e-mail
YouTube link to the Final Presentation

Keywords: Include a list of keywords that best categorize your work. Some organizations, such as ACM, have a classification index from which keywords and subject areas are chosen.

Project Overview: Include the project name and description, project goals and objectives, project scope, and team members and their roles and responsibilities.

Deliverables: List all completed deliverables and functional specifications. Include current project status. The remaining work and backlog items are known issues and risks.

Technical Details: Include the following:
Codebase overview (repositories, branches, version control)
Key dependencies and libraries
Deployment instructions (environment details, configuration)
Database schema and data migration details
Software architecture

Testing Information: Include the following:
Summary of testing conducted (unit, integration, system, acceptance)
Test cases and results
Outstanding bugs and defect log

User Documentation: Provide user guides, manuals, workflows, screenshots, training materials, and FAQs.

Transition Plan/Next Steps: Include knowledge transfer activities and a sustainability plan for the project. (You may need to consult your advisor for their insight on next steps.)

Acknowledgments: Acknowledge any individuals who have helped you during the course of the project, including your project advisor. If you have been supported by a company or a scholarship/fellowship, then this should also be acknowledged.

Appendices: Include brief code fragments and illustrations of results that are too verbose for the body of your report. Reference these in the body of your report. If you have a lot of raw data that you think might be interesting, you can place examples of that here as well.

Biography: Include a biography of each team member, places where they have worked, and state your goals for employment or graduate study. A brief sentence about your personal interests can always be included at the end of your biography, as that helps to personalize your work and can orient others toward you as an individual.
*/

#import "../style.typ": report

#show: report

#include "title-page.typ"
#pagebreak()
#include "overview.typ"
#include "deli.typ"
#include "tech.typ"
#include "ack.typ"
#include "appendix.typ"
#include "bio.typ"
